{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when","id":1189761,"title":"Deviant: The Renegades, when?!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-26T21:00:11-08:00","id":1189761,"title":"Deviant: The Renegades, when?!","content":"When I get the newsletter, the first thing I look at is Deviant: The Renegades status.... again .... since forever.<br /> <br /> I pretty much have all the books since White wolf and have started replacing them with digital copies so I'm pretty invested.<br /> <br /> I remember the excitement I felt when something new came out, Werewolf when I had Vampire, Geist, Beast the Primordial.<br /> <br /> When I look at the current production schedule I can't help but be disappointed by all the rehashing of all the same old stuff. Vampires in the dark ages? OK, but several books about it?<br /> <br /> I'm sure it's all good, but if you could shunt at least half your resources to previously announced (years ago) product it would be appreciated and I can't help feeling a good business move as well. I can't be the only one.<br /> <br /> Thank You for Your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T21:30:47-08:00","id":1189771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when#post1189761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I look at the current production schedule I can't help but be disappointed by all the rehashing of all the same old stuff. <b>Vampires in the dark ages? OK, but several books about it?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>...what? No there isn't.<br /> <br /> All of the Dark Ages Vampire20 books have been released a while ago. And while never-say-never, but with VtM5e coming up there's unlikely to be more books within WoD20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure it's all good, but if you could shunt at least half your resources to previously announced (years ago) product it would be appreciated and I can't help feeling a good business move as well. I can't be the only one. </div> </div> </div>The gamelines move at different paces due to a variety of complicated factors. From differing workflows of the line devs, to writers/artists/editors taking their time to make sure their end of the product is going smoothly, to any other real-life issues that could be involved in slowing things down. We don't know. And OPP isn't obligated to telling us on every single little thing that happens.<br /> <br /> Just because your favorite gameline isn't having a whole lot of development doesn't mean that other people's gamelines should be sidelined instead.<br /> <br /> Throwing more money at it won't make things move faster. It'll be ready when it's ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T22:42:18-08:00","id":1189785,"title":"","content":"It's not so much my favorite gameline as the company not releasing new product while rehashing old stuff.<br /> <br /> Pumping out a new line every few years is good for everyone.<br /> <br /> If a few Vampire books need to be delayed to do that so be it, we have way more than enough.<br /> <br /> And you are correct, it's M20 stuff now not Dark Ages, that's how long we've been waiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","user":"Thlaylie","date":". 02-27-2018, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T23:00:43-08:00","id":1189788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1189785#post1189785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much my favorite gameline as the company not releasing new product while rehashing old stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rehashing WHAT old stuff?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a few Vampire books need to be delayed to do that so be it, we have way more than enough. </div> </div> </div>Once again, all of the gamelines are developed by different people at different paces. What happens in one gameline does NOT affect what happens in another. And it's incredibly silly and counter-productive to artificially slow down what happens in another gameline to speed up another. That's not how things work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you are correct, it's M20 stuff now not Dark Ages, that's how long we've been waiting. </div> </div> </div>...which is not remotely comparable considering what we know of how M20 is written for. That they're largely written by the line developer, especially with stuff like the upcoming Gods and Monsters. The line developer, who last I checked, is not involved in any way with Deviant.<br /> <br /> So no. Slowing down Mage20 stuff is not going to make Deviant arrive faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 02-27-2018, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T00:19:16-08:00","id":1189796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when#post1189761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When I get the newsletter, the first thing I look at is Deviant: The Renegades status.... again .... since forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad that you\u2019re so enthusiastic, Thlaylie, but Deviant is still in first drafts. From my experience in this process, and it being a core book for a new line, I wouldn\u2019t expect to see it for another 9-12 months. (Not speaking in any official capacity, just what I\u2019ve seen of how the process works.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T02:20:34-08:00","id":1189812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1189785#post1189785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pumping out a new line every few years is good for everyone.<br /> <br /> If a few Vampire books need to be delayed to do that so be it, we have way more than enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this statement completely. Having only 4 books in Vampire (sorry, I don't use first edition books), I'm annoyed that Onyx path is pouring resources into completely new lines while &quot;ignoring&quot; the established ones.<br /> <br /> I know I'm exaggerating slightly, however I just want to point out, that there are people who disagree with &quot;pumping out a new line is good for everyone&quot;. Especially if that means delaying books for already established lines, which you seem to be in favor of.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T06:22:25-08:00","id":1189851,"title":"","content":"All of us want more stuff for the lines we are more interested about. I have my horses in this race, but that's a sentiment that pops up everywhere, understandably so.<br /> <br /> I personally prefer to avoid knowing about the behind the scenes, an attitude that's well worth a relative ignorance for the peace of mind it grants me, but I'm quite sure it's not as simple as some books getting favored above others. Lots of factor behind it, but each game has its developers and writers and a lot of possible complications that might slow down the process.<br /> <br /> Not gonna lie, there's a side of me that screams &quot;Conspiracy! Conspiracy against what I like!&quot; every now and then, but then the rational mind kicks in and I aknowledge things are less dramatic than that. It's just the state of things being more complex and less smooth than we imagine.<br /> <br /> I'm saying this as someone really looking forward to Deviant, since what I know about it made me save some money for a Kickstarter ages ago, so I feel you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-27-2018, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T07:22:39-08:00","id":1189857,"title":"","content":"Vampire has not had a resourcing impact on Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:26:15-08:00","id":1189891,"title":"","content":"Slow and steady wins the race I rather wait for a great polished product . Then instantly get a mediocre product","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T14:13:06-08:00","id":1190005,"title":"","content":"The term &quot;old stuff&quot; applies to existing repeated lines like Vampire owod, nwod, cod, V20, dark ages etc. I dont mean to pick on vampire specifically, but as the first it has the most books.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the overwhelming defense of Onyx, but as a customer I feel I have the right to express my opinion.<br /> <br /> In my point of view, after reviewing all the offered material available I have determined that all I need is the core books of the CoD which I have. I'm waiting (and waiting) for another new line core book.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just me, but I can't be the only customer that feels that way. If you are running a business you don't just tell a customer to wait while you pump out your preferred product. I have no way of knowing that this is what they are doing, but it seems to me it's much easier to write for existing lines than make something new. I'm just asking for a bit of consideration while hopefully possibly showing Onyx that they have fallen into this rut.(If they have)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T15:57:46-08:00","id":1190039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1190005#post1190005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term &quot;old stuff&quot; applies to existing repeated lines like Vampire owod, nwod, cod, V20, dark ages etc. I dont mean to pick on vampire specifically, but as the first it has the most books.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's the most popular. Makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, this is just me, but I can't be the only customer that feels that way. </div> </div> </div>You're not the only customer either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you are running a business you don't just tell a customer to wait while you pump out your preferred product. </div> </div> </div>Yeah you do.<br /> <br /> Because products take time to make. They can't just crank out a book within a month, and if you expect said book to be a quality product.<br /> <br /> These. Things. Take. Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T17:57:49-08:00","id":1190078,"title":"","content":"Additionally:<br /> <br /> These books rarely impact each other. As has been stated. If Vampire books are coming out, that's because the development team (and related teams) have completed them. Unless there is a resource bottleneck, what one development team is doing has no bearing on the others.<br /> <br /> New lines and edition update take longer than supplements, because they have more moving parts and things to balance (like theme, cohesive mechanics, etc.).<br /> <br /> And if you want to talk about waiting for something, go into the Mage sub-forum and compare Signs of Sorcery. Point is: Things get developed on different schedules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T18:02:17-08:00","id":1190081,"title":"","content":"Aka: good things come to those who wait. Trust me, words to live by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T04:46:38-08:00","id":1190203,"title":"","content":"I'm also waiting for Deviant, and boy did I wait for Beast, but to sum up what has been pointed out numerous times:<br /> - these things take (a lot of!) time<br /> - new lines take longer, because you cannot build on pre-existing themes/concepts/mechanics<br /> - other products are just as eagerly awaited by other people (go and ask how many people are dying to get the Beast- Player's Guide, and then compare with Signs of Sorcery. Then ask Geist-fans how much they care about those when they're eagerly awaiting their 2nd Ed upgrade)<br /> - that isn't a problem though, because what the Mage team does doesn't have a bearing on the Deviant team's work (and even the people working on one Vampire book might be independent from the development of other Vampire books)<br /> - many people don't care about new gamelines, instead prefering more books on existing gamelines (just go to werewolf and read the claims of 'W:tF has been abandoned' because there hasn't been a 2ed Book in a while, then ask yourself what they would prefer: Deviant or new WtF books?)<br /> - Yes, you have a right to express your opinion. So do others. None of this makes anyone 'right'.<br /> <br /> One more thing, though: it may be due to my reading of your answers, but I get a vibe of 'I am entitled to that gameline, because it has been promised'. If this is not at all what you are feeling, I apologize full-heartedly in advance. However, since this is a personal pet peeve of mine: <i>None of us </i>have a 'right' to new books or gamelines. OPP is still a business, which means to keep producing, they have to make a winning somewhere, otherwise they'd have to stop producing completely, which would suck immensely. Even if they <i>would </i>decide to slow down the development of Deviant to save on resources in favour of other gamelines, it'd be <i>their </i>call to make. We could be unhappy with it, yeah, but there wouldn't be any sense in complaining about it, and it would be preferable to the alternative.<br /> Bottom line: Try to be patient, because otherwise, you're just going to make waiting harder on yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T06:05:26-08:00","id":1190233,"title":"","content":"New gamelines are also harder because everything needs to be on point. Vampire, Mage and Werewolf can endure a not-so-perfect supplement here and there, but if a core for a new game (or a smaller gameline book) has issues it's gonna make everything more difficult from the start and require some adjustments with following books, which makes things even more complicated.<br /> <br /> Keep that in mind, I find it helps a lot","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-28-2018, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T10:10:59-08:00","id":1190320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1190005#post1190005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term &amp;quot;old stuff&amp;quot; applies to existing repeated lines like Vampire owod, nwod, cod, V20, dark ages etc. I dont mean to pick on vampire specifically, but as the first it has the most books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, there\u2019s just as much old stuff in just as much of a content drought. And the existing lines already have established fan bases who also feel their favorite game is being ignored in favor of others. This exact conversation comes up every couple of months in one subforum or another, about one gameline or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1190005#post1190005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the overwhelming defense of Onyx, but as a customer I feel I have the right to express my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is telling you you don\u2019t have the right to express your opinion (provided you do so respectfully, of course). We are merely pointing out that your concerns are a little misguided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1190005#post1190005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my point of view, after reviewing all the offered material available I have determined that all I need is the core books of the CoD which I have. I'm waiting (and waiting) for another new line core book.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just me, but I can't be the only customer that feels that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sure you\u2019re not. But there are just as many, probably more, who would rather they just work on the already ongoing lines and not make new ones. Just a few days ago we had someone complaining that Deviant was taking up too much of Dave\u2019s time when he should be working on Mage. Dave is damned if he does, damned if he doesn\u2019t here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1190005#post1190005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are running a business you don't just tell a customer to wait while you pump out your preferred product. I have no way of knowing that this is what they are doing, but it seems to me it's much easier to write for existing lines than make something new. I'm just asking for a bit of consideration while hopefully possibly showing Onyx that they have fallen into this rut.(If they have)</div> </div> </div> </div>They haven\u2019t. They don\u2019t just work on one thing at a time. Deviant is being worked on <i>alongside</i> various other gamelines, by different development teams. A given line having more supplements doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s getting more attention or resources dedicated to it than others. There are an incredible number of unpredictable variables involved in getting these books made, sometimes a book takes longer than others, and there is nothing we can do to influence that.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sorry you are feeling so frustrated with the wait for Deviant. But waiting is really all we can do. Complaining that other game lines are getting books while Deviant hasn\u2019t been finished yet will not help Deviant get finished any faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T10:43:01-08:00","id":1190332,"title":"","content":"Yeah member when people bitched about Beast that as a designer seed was a little under backed they do NOT want to deal witch the stress of that I see the same complaining in the light novel fandom why do the take 4 mouths this shitty google translate version was out a day after the Japanese release why can\u2019t you release a book every week why are they so expensive,they not that in Japan because of course light novels have the same amount of poplurarty as in Japan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T16:26:33-08:00","id":1190478,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your responses. I guess I just wanted to be heard.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I sounded gruff, I work in Law Enforcement and have been told I come off that way. I felt a bit attacked by the aggressive responses to my post. Sorry if some felt their world was being attacked.<br /> <br /> I will wait patiently for Deviant to come out now that I've had my say. It was just bugging me forever, but now I feel better with an informed response.<br /> <br /> Thank You.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","user":"Thlaylie","date":". 02-28-2018, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:03:05-08:00","id":1190648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1190478#post1190478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you all for your responses. I guess I just wanted to be heard.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I sounded gruff, I work in Law Enforcement and have been told I come off that way. I felt a bit attacked by the aggressive responses to my post. Sorry if some felt their world was being attacked.<br /> <br /> I will wait patiently for Deviant to come out now that I've had my say. It was just bugging me forever, but now I feel better with an informed response.<br /> <br /> Thank You.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's cool, it's frustration that comes from love for the books and wanting more. We all get there sometimes, don't worry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T10:09:01-08:00","id":1190703,"title":"","content":"Just wishing we had another <s>hit</s>dev blog post to tide us over...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T12:42:33-08:00","id":1191086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1190478#post1190478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you all for your responses. I guess I just wanted to be heard.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I sounded gruff, I work in Law Enforcement and have been told I come off that way. I felt a bit attacked by the aggressive responses to my post. Sorry if some felt their world was being attacked.<br /> <br /> I will wait patiently for Deviant to come out now that I've had my say. It was just bugging me forever, but now I feel better with an informed response.<br /> <br /> Thank You.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, no worries. Sorry if my post made you feel attacked - wasn't my intention.<br /> The desire to be heard is entirely normal, especially when there is a long waiting period involved and one just wants some additional information. We've al been there, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> <br /> mentioned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> I second that =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:06:36-07:00","id":1194535,"title":"","content":"I know how you feel, though in my case it's waiting on 2E of Hunter: The Vigil(unless that came out and slipped under my nose). Though in my case I just want the core rule book, the Vampire and Werewolf core books, Hunter and Hunter Supplements. And while I would like a steady source of news or information, I understand that also would probably slow things down. I think it's just a matter of perception, things just seem to take longer when we want them but I'm sure there were plenty of people eagerly awaiting those vampire books and annoyed at all the other things that came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T20:02:15-07:00","id":1199926,"title":"","content":"Deviant made Redlines!<br /> <br /> Whoot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T04:16:14-07:00","id":1200384,"title":"","content":"Just for the record, Redlines are more of less the equivalent of &quot;first tested Alpha version&quot;, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T05:39:38-07:00","id":1200396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1200384#post1200384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, Redlines are more of less the equivalent of &amp;quot;first tested Alpha version&amp;quot;, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think it is more &quot;here is everything the writers wrote, now let's make sure it fits together&quot;. Pre-Alpha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-28-2018, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T08:00:51-07:00","id":1200431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1189761-deviant-the-renegades-when?p=1200384#post1200384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the record, Redlines are more of less the equivalent of &amp;quot;first tested Alpha version&amp;quot;, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Redlines is the part where all the first drafts are in, and the developer reads over everything to make sure that it all fits together properly, noting places where things need changing or clarification. After that, the drafts and the notes are sent back to the writers so that they can write the next draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}